Now that we have the simplified forms for $14x(19-7x)$ and $(19-7x)^2$, let's combine them with $49x^2$ to find the simplified form of the entire expression:

\begin{align*}
49x^2+14x(19-7x)+(19-7x)^2&=49x^2+(266x-98x^2)+(361-98x+49x^2)\\
&=49x^2-98x^2+266x-98x+361\\
&=\boxed{361+168x}
\end{align*}

So, the simplified form of the entire expression is $361+168x$.
